@namespace NoBorders.Components.Screens
@using NoBorders
@* Stub per Phase 2.6's scope ("stub views for Permissions/About") — unlike
   Permissions, there's no existing feature or design mockup to source
   content from here, so this stays deliberately minimal: app identity
   only. Description text is design-handoff/README.md's own description
   of the app, not invented copy.

   Icon: Borderless Gaming App UI/icon_export's 64-grid violet mark
   (noborders-256-violet.svg, copied to wwwroot/img/noborders-mark-large.svg)
   — the smooth full-detail source, not the 16-grid pixel mark the header
   bars use, per that icon set's own README ("Use at 24 px and above").

   Version: reads NoBorders.AppVersion (program.cs) — the real assembly
   version — instead of a hardcoded string. Was a leftover "v2.4" from the
   original design mockup that never matched the actual build (1.0.0) and
   would only drift further with each future release; see AppVersion's own
   doc comment. *@

<div class="nb-about-page__header">
    <img src="/img/noborders-mark-large.svg" alt="" class="nb-about-page__icon" />
    <div>
        <div class="nb-about-page__title">NoBorders</div>
        <div class="nb-about-page__version nb-mono">@AppVersion.Display</div>
    </div>
</div>
<div class="nb-about-page__description">A Windows borderless-window manager for games.</div>
